          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal declarative directly avows the narrator's present loving emotional state toward Maria. Its solemn framing strengthens its presentation as true, especially as it answers her concern that his apparent change may be temporary.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The exact focal expression asserts love but does not itself undertake an action, obligation, or defined relational commitment. The surrounding turn contains separate future-oriented language about living with Maria, but that undertaking should not be transferred to the marked avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is intensely emotional, the focal words occur in a deliberate answer to Maria's question and function as an assertion of love, not as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"No core force remains inadequately represented by T/P/E. The expression answers and reassures Maria, but it does so through the direct avowal captured by T rather than through a distinct residual mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent change is genuine and lasting rather than something he will regret tomorrow. He answers her face to face with the marked declaration of love, embedded in a longer explanation of what he loves about her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself contains no undertaking. A separate neighbouring statement—\\\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\\\"—expresses an intended long shared life, but its precise practical terms are unspecified. Maria's immediate uptake of the overall reply is belief and happiness: the narration says that she understands he is speaking truthfully. The evidence does not present a separate explicit acceptance of defined commitments.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not confidently recognise the work from the supplied passages.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly supports the represented sincerity of this avowal, but it does not specify concrete terms for a relationship undertaking or establish what later occurs. The classification therefore keeps the focal avowal distinct from the future-oriented sentences elsewhere in the same turn.\"}"
